(Bug #86's working neighbour, kept working. A float with NO precision
 already rendered identically in every sink, through a different
 routine (`_buffer_append_float`), and the fix for the precision arm
 must leave that one alone: the trimmed default rendering, its
 always-present decimal point, its sign, and the magnitudes past 2^63.

 The other specifiers already held parity too - radix and integer width
 render the same in Print, in a text and in a buffer - so they are here
 for the same reason: the arm that was added must not have moved them.)

a float called ratio is 2.5.
a float called owed is -1.25.
a float called whole is 3.0.
a float called 'ten sextillion' is 10000000000000000000000.0.

Print "print:  {ratio} {owed} {whole} {ten sextillion}".

a text called said is "text:   {ratio} {owed} {whole} {ten sextillion}".
Print said.

Create a buffer called built.
copy "buffer: {ratio} {owed} {whole} {ten sextillion}" to built.
Print built.

Open a file at 1 for writing called out.
write "write:  {ratio} {owed} {whole} {ten sextillion}\n" to out.

a number called count is 255.

Print "print:  {count} {count:x} {count:06} {count:o} {count:b}".

a text called counted is "text:   {count} {count:x} {count:06} {count:o} {count:b}".
Print counted.

Create a buffer called tallied.
copy "buffer: {count} {count:x} {count:06} {count:o} {count:b}" to tallied.
Print tallied.

write "write:  {count} {count:x} {count:06} {count:o} {count:b}\n" to out.
